---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Aegis-Beacon | Open Source Emergency Radio System"
  description="Low-cost emergency radio-location system based on LoRa for mountain rescue and SAR operations."
>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     HERO - asymmetric split: editorial copy + real device
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<div class="hero-wrap">
  <section class="hero-section container">
    <div class="hero-grid">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="hero-kicker">Open-source LoRa emergency radio</p>
        <h1 class="hero-title">A rescue beacon that broadcasts your position when every network is gone.</h1>
        <p class="hero-sub">
          Radio-location system for mountain rescue and SAR teams, built from
          off-the-shelf parts. No GSM, no subscriptions, no network to transmit.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a href="/wiki" class="btn btn-primary">Read the docs</a>
          <a href="/demo" class="btn btn-secondary">Try the live demo</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-device" data-rv="scale">
        <div class="device-frame">
          <div class="device-frame__bar">
            <span class="device-frame__title">AEGIS-BEACON</span>
            <span class="device-frame__status">TX ACTIVE</span>
          </div>
          <img src="/banner.png" alt="Aegis-Beacon emergency radio device" class="device-image" loading="eager" width="1200" height="600" />
        </div>
        <dl class="spec-rail">
          <div class="spec-rail__item"><dt>BOM</dt><dd>$23-28</dd></div>
          <div class="spec-rail__item"><dt>Band</dt><dd>410-525 MHz</dd></div>
          <div class="spec-rail__item"><dt>Runtime</dt><dd>65h+</dd></div>
          <div class="spec-rail__item"><dt>Range</dt><dd>15 km</dd></div>
          <div class="spec-rail__item"><dt>Deep sleep</dt><dd>10 uA</dd></div>
          <div class="spec-rail__item"><dt>Modes</dt><dd>4</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     FIELD - the device in context
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="section container" data-rv>
  <div class="banner-showcase">
    <div class="banner-img-wrap" data-parallax="0.14">
      <img src="/banner.png" alt="Aegis-Beacon emergency radio device in the field" class="banner-image" loading="lazy" />
    </div>
    <div class="banner-overlay">
      <p class="banner-caption">Aegis-Beacon v5.4, built for those who save lives</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     DESIGN - why it is built this way (asymmetric)
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="section container">
  <header class="section-head section-head--left" data-rv>
    <h2 class="section-head__title">Designed around one job: being found</h2>
    <p class="section-head__lead">Every component and every line of firmware exists to get your position to a rescuer, with nothing left to fail.</p>
  </header>

  <div class="design-grid" data-rv>
    <article class="design-card design-card--wide">
      <h3>Long-range radio link</h3>
      <p>SX1262 transceiver with a +30 dBm power amplifier reaches up to 15 km line-of-sight across the 410-525 MHz band. The firmware sweeps a preloaded frequency list, so a rescuer with a cheap SDR will hear the beacon.</p>
      <div class="design-card__code" aria-hidden="true">
        <span class="dim">TX 433.500 MHz</span>
        <span class="accent">SOS ··· --- ···</span>
        <span class="dim">+17 dBm CW</span>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="design-card">
      <h3>Ultra-low power</h3>
      <p>Deep sleep at 10 uA with a 30-second hardware watchdog. WiFi and Bluetooth are disabled in beacon mode, pushing runtime past 65 hours on a single 18650 cell.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="design-card">
      <h3>No infrastructure</h3>
      <p>Direct peer-to-peer radio. No GSM, WiFi, or satellite link is required, so the beacon works in canyons, forests, and anywhere cellular coverage ends.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="design-card">
      <h3>Open source, MIT</h3>
      <p>Firmware, schematics, and the full bill of materials are MIT licensed and built with PlatformIO. Anyone can inspect, modify, and verify the rescue logic.</p>
    </article>

    <article class="design-card">
      <h3>GPS-aware beaconing</h3>
      <p>The NEO-6M GPS module encodes coordinates directly into the Morse payload, so search teams receive a position without any proprietary protocol.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     MODES - console-style rows (no numbered cards)
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="section section-alt">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="section-head section-head--left" data-rv>
      <h2 class="section-head__title">Four operating modes</h2>
      <p class="section-head__lead">A single button cycles the device between beacon, search, configuration, and emergency transmission.</p>
    </header>

    <div class="modes-console" data-rv>
      <div class="mode-row">
        <div class="mode-row__name">BEACON</div>
        <p class="mode-row__desc">Transmits Morse SOS with GPS coordinates on all configured frequencies, then enters a deep-sleep cycle for maximum runtime.</p>
        <dl class="mode-row__meta">
          <div><dt>TX</dt><dd>+17 dBm</dd></div>
          <div><dt>LED</dt><dd>Red</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div class="mode-row">
        <div class="mode-row__name">SEARCH</div>
        <p class="mode-row__desc">Scans every frequency sequentially and measures RSSI on each, with a rising-pitch audio alert when a signal is detected.</p>
        <dl class="mode-row__meta">
          <div><dt>RX</dt><dd>Scan</dd></div>
          <div><dt>LED</dt><dd>Blue</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div class="mode-row">
        <div class="mode-row__name">CONFIG</div>
        <p class="mode-row__desc">WiFi access point with a captive-portal dashboard. Adjust frequency, WPM, power, and GPS settings from a browser, no reflash.</p>
        <dl class="mode-row__meta">
          <div><dt>Net</dt><dd>WiFi AP</dd></div>
          <div><dt>LED</dt><dd>Both</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
      <div class="mode-row">
        <div class="mode-row__name">EMERGENCY</div>
        <p class="mode-row__desc">Maximum power, continuous transmission, full payload. No deep sleep. A 1760 Hz audible tone for critical rescue situations.</p>
        <dl class="mode-row__meta">
          <div><dt>TX</dt><dd>+22 dBm</dd></div>
          <div><dt>LED</dt><dd>Fast</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     STACK - single mono rail, no chips
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="section container">
  <header class="section-head section-head--left" data-rv>
    <h2 class="section-head__title">Industry-standard components</h2>
  </header>
  <div class="stack-rail" data-rv>
    <span>ESP32</span><span>SX1262</span><span>SSD1309</span><span>NEO-6M</span><span>RadioLib</span><span>PlatformIO</span>
  </div>
  <p class="stack-note">Six parts. Every one chosen for availability and long production lifetime.</p>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     FAQ
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="section section-alt">
  <div class="container">
    <header class="section-head section-head--left" data-rv>
      <h2 class="section-head__title">Frequently asked questions</h2>
    </header>
    <div class="faq">
      <details class="faq__item" name="faq" data-rv="fade">
        <summary class="faq__question">
          <span>What is the total cost to build an Aegis-Beacon?</span>
          <svg class="faq__chevron" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M7 7L10 10L13 7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <p class="faq__answer">The complete bill of materials costs between $23 and $28 depending on sourcing. All components are readily available from AliExpress or local electronics stores. No specialized tools beyond a soldering iron are needed.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq__item" name="faq" data-rv="fade">
        <summary class="faq__question">
          <span>Does it require any cellular or internet connection?</span>
          <svg class="faq__chevron" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M7 7L10 10L13 7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <p class="faq__answer">No. Aegis-Beacon uses direct peer-to-peer LoRa radio communication. It works entirely offline. No GSM, WiFi, or satellite subscription is needed for emergency beacon operation. WiFi is only used in Config mode for local settings adjustment.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq__item" name="faq" data-rv="fade">
        <summary class="faq__question">
          <span>What is the maximum range?</span>
          <svg class="faq__chevron" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M7 7L10 10L13 7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <p class="faq__answer">Up to 15 km line-of-sight with the included antenna at +17 dBm TX power. In Emergency mode, continuous transmission at +22 dBm extends range further. Real-world range depends on terrain, obstacles, and antenna orientation.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq__item" name="faq" data-rv="fade">
        <summary class="faq__question">
          <span>How long does the battery last?</span>
          <svg class="faq__chevron" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M7 7L10 10L13 7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <p class="faq__answer">In Beacon mode with a standard 18650 cell (3000 mAh), expect 65+ hours of continuous operation. The device enters deep sleep at 10 uA between transmissions, maximizing battery life for extended rescue operations.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq__item" name="faq" data-rv="fade">
        <summary class="faq__question">
          <span>Is this legal to use?</span>
          <svg class="faq__chevron" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M7 7L10 10L13 7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <p class="faq__answer">The device operates in the 410-525 MHz band. Check your local regulations for unlicensed radio operation. In many jurisdictions, low-power emergency beacons are permitted. The firmware supports PMR446-compliant frequencies.</p>
      </details>
      <details class="faq__item" name="faq" data-rv="fade">
        <summary class="faq__question">
          <span>How do I configure the device?</span>
          <svg class="faq__chevron" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 20 20" fill="none"><path d="M7 7L10 10L13 7" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/></svg>
        </summary>
        <p class="faq__answer">Switch to Config mode to activate the WiFi Access Point. Connect to "AEGIS-SETUP" and open 192.168.4.1 in your browser. The captive portal lets you adjust every parameter without reflashing the firmware.</p>
      </details>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
     CTA
     ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
<section class="cta-section" data-rv>
  <div class="cta-inner container">
    <h2>Built in the open, for the field</h2>
    <p>Follow the build guide, plan your bill of materials, and assemble your own rescue beacon.</p>
    <div class="cta-buttons">
      <a href="/builder" class="btn btn-cta">Plan your build</a>
      <a href="https://github.com/Leo-Galli/Aegis-Beacon" target="_blank" rel="noopener" class="btn btn-cta-ghost">Star on GitHub</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
</Layout>